+# Customers: customer-manager saves a note on a customer
+
+## Application Overview
+
+Ticket 06. A staff member who can only manage customers (actor "customer" = user.manager@example.com, populatedb's single-permission customer-management group) opens the "orders" scenario customer Ada Lovelace (CUSTOMER constant, e2e.customer@example.com), writes a note, saves the page, and the note is saved: the field shows it after saving and still shows it after a reload.
+
+Target spec: e2e/tests/customers/customer-note.spec.ts. Exactly one test (the happy path covering all three acceptance criteria). It must NOT run as the superuser.
+
+Spec setup (required):
+- `import { expect, test } from "../../fixtures/test.ts";`
+- `import { CUSTOMER, ORDERS_SCENARIO } from "../../scenarios/orders.ts";` - reuse CUSTOMER.email / firstName / lastName, never hardcode the email.
+- `test.use({ scenario: ORDERS_SCENARIO, actor: "customer" });` - Ada only exists in the "orders" scenario (built on "default"), and "customer" maps to user.manager@example.com in e2e/lib/actors.ts. The fixture restores the database before the test, so no cleanup is needed.
+- `// Arrange`, `// Act`, `// Assert` comments (as in order-creation.spec.ts: `// Act & Assert` around test.step blocks is acceptable); one test.step per stage; tag the title with #e2e like the order specs.
+- Note: e2e/tests/seed.spec.ts signs in as admin on the "default" scenario; it was only used for exploring the UI. Exploration was also repeated signed in as user.manager@example.com and the full flow succeeded for that account (on a populatedb customer, since Ada is not in "default"). Observed: that account's token reports userPermissions [MANAGE_USERS, IMPERSONATE_USER]. The sidebar shows only Home, Customers (All) and Extensions; the user menu shows "William Archer".
+
+Page object (new, e2e/pages/customerPage.ts; readonly fields initialised from this.page, empty `constructor(readonly page: Page) {}`; locators were checked against the live dashboard):
+- searchInput = page.getByTestId("search-input")  (textbox "Search customers" on /customers/; typing updates the URL with ?query=<email>)
+- list = page.getByTestId("list")  (customers datagrid wrapper)
+- gridCanvas = page.locator('[data-testid="data-grid-canvas"]')  (Glide datagrid canvas; note Glide uses data-testid, not the dashboard's data-test-id, so getByTestId does not match it)
+- result cell for waiting: page.getByRole("gridcell", { name: CUSTOMER.email }) / locator('[role="gridcell"]', { hasText: email }) - cells live in Glide's accessibility table (ids glide-cell-<col>-<row>), attached but not clickable
+- rowAnchor = page.getByTestId("datagrid-row-anchor")  (gets href /customers/<id>? on row hover)
+- firstNameInput = getByTestId("customer-first-name"), lastNameInput = getByTestId("customer-last-name"), emailInput = getByTestId("customer-email")  (labels "First Name", "Last Name", "Email address" in the "Contact" card, data-test-id="customer-details")
+- noteInput = page.getByTestId("customer-note")  - a <textarea name="note">, accessible name/label "Note" (getByRole("textbox", { name: "Note" }) also works)
+- saveButton = page.getByTestId("button-bar-confirm")  (Savebar "Save"; disabled until the form is dirty, disabled again after a successful save/reload)
+- backButton = page.getByTestId("button-bar-cancel")  ("Back")
+- notification = page.getByRole("region", { name: /Notifications/ }).getByRole("listitem")  - success toast reads title "Success", text "Customer updated" (src/customers/views/CustomerDetails.tsx, message id PeEood). The ticket's example "Saved changes" is NOT what this page shows; assert on "Customer updated".
+
+Opening a row: Glide renders rows on a canvas that an overlay div (.dvn-scroller) covers, so locator.click()/hover() on the canvas or gridcell fails with "intercepts pointer events". After the search narrows the grid to one row, click by coordinates: `const box = await gridCanvas.boundingBox(); await page.mouse.click(box.x + 200, box.y + box.height - 20);` (header row plus one data row, canvas height ~82px), then `page.waitForURL(u => /\/customers\/[^/]+$/.test(u.pathname))`. Alternatively hover the row with page.mouse.move and click the datagrid-row-anchor. (The legacy BasePage.clickGridCell fiber hack is the fallback if coordinates prove flaky.)
+
+Customer-manager view of the details page (useful to prove the actor): "Total orders", "Recent total", "Avg order value" tiles, the "Recent Orders" card and the "Gift cards" card are hidden for this actor (admin sees them); "Last login", "Attributes", "Contact" and "Address Information" are present.
+
+## Test Scenarios
+
+### 1. Customer note (customer-manager actor, orders scenario)
+
+**Seed:** `e2e/tests/seed.spec.ts`
+
+#### 1.1. Customer manager saves a note on a customer and it persists after reload #e2e
+
+**File:** `e2e/tests/customers/customer-note.spec.ts`
+
+**Steps:**
+  1. Arrange: the spec declares test.use({ scenario: ORDERS_SCENARIO, actor: "customer" }) so the database is restored to the "orders" scenario and the browser is signed in as user.manager@example.com (customer management only, not the superuser). Define a unique note text in the test body, e.g. const note = "Prefers a phone call before any order is shipped."; instantiate new CustomerPage(page).
+    - expect: No UI login is performed; the stored session for the "customer" actor is used
+    - expect: The test does not use the admin actor
+  2. test.step "find the customer from the customers list": go to /customers/ and wait for the search input (getByTestId("search-input")). Fill it with CUSTOMER.email.
+    - expect: The URL gains query=e2e.customer%40example.com
+    - expect: Exactly one grid row is shown, with a gridcell containing CUSTOMER.email (and one containing `${CUSTOMER.firstName} ${CUSTOMER.lastName}`, i.e. "Ada Lovelace")
+    - expect: The sidebar has no Catalog/Fulfillment/Discounts entries, confirming the restricted actor (optional sanity check)
+  3. test.step "open the customer": click the single result row on the datagrid canvas by coordinates (page.mouse.click inside the data-grid-canvas bounding box, below the header row), then wait for the URL /customers/<id>.
+    - expect: The details page loads, titled with the customer's email
+    - expect: getByTestId("customer-email") has value CUSTOMER.email
+    - expect: getByTestId("customer-first-name") has value CUSTOMER.firstName and getByTestId("customer-last-name") has value CUSTOMER.lastName
+    - expect: The Note field (getByTestId("customer-note"), label "Note") is visible and editable
+    - expect: The Save button (getByTestId("button-bar-confirm")) is disabled before any edit
+  4. test.step "write a note and save": fill the Note textarea with the note text, then click Save (button-bar-confirm).
+    - expect: Save becomes enabled after filling the note
+    - expect: After clicking Save, a notification appears in the "Notifications" region with "Success" and "Customer updated"
+    - expect: No error notification is shown
+  5. test.step "the note field shows the new note": read the Note field immediately after the save confirmation.
+    - expect: expect(noteInput).toHaveValue(note) - acceptance criterion 2
+    - expect: The Save button is disabled again (form no longer dirty)
+  6. test.step "the note survives a reload": page.reload(), wait for the Note field to be visible.
+    - expect: expect(noteInput).toHaveValue(note) after reload - acceptance criterion 3, proving the note was persisted on the customer server-side
+    - expect: The page still shows CUSTOMER.email in the email field (same customer)
+    - expect: The Save button is disabled
